  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Policy and Systems Research responding to the climate crises: lessons from countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A collaboration between the World Health Organization (WHO) Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research (AHPSR) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) to support a call for proposals for low- and middle-income country (LMIC) case studies examining how health systems are responding to the climate crisis at the national or sub-national levels. Informed by  qualitative data from key country stakeholders, research teams will develop analytical case studies in collaboration with national policy-makers as they attempt to adapt to, mitigate and build broader resilience to the ongoing climate crisis.

This collaboration will support a total of twelve country case studies and associated costs for the Alliance secretariat.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">These country case studies will:
- Identify and document  examples where health  system policymakers  and managers are actively responding to climate change, trying to mitigate climate change, as well as adapting  health systems and  improving  health policies and broader  resilience in collaboration with national health policymakers; 
- Share lessons from countries across WHO regions; 
- Synthesize evidence  contributing to the  development of improved guidance on  how countries can overcome existing barriers, respond to the climate crisis and move towards climate-resilient and low carbon sustainable health systems.</narrative>
  </description>
